WEBVTT

00:00:13.962 --> 00:00:19.023
Cheetah presents Hamlet Prince of Denmark by William Shakespeare.

00:00:19.043 --> 00:00:22.124
One.

00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:32.597
The Ghost.

00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:48.844
One night at Elsinore Castle in Denmark, two guards see a ghost.

00:00:48.904 --> 00:00:54.478
It looks like King Hamlet.

00:00:54.538 --> 00:00:56.678
But it can't be!

00:00:56.738 --> 00:00:58.860
King Hamlet is dead!

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.012
We must tell Horatio, Prince Hamlet's friend.

00:01:03.072 --> 00:01:09.607
Perhaps the ghost wants to give a message to the prince.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:16.451
The next night Horatio stays to watch with the guards.

00:01:16.511 --> 00:01:19.692
The ghost appears again.

00:01:19.752 --> 00:01:25.044
It is wearing the same armour as the old king.

00:01:25.104 --> 00:01:28.015
What do you want?

00:01:28.075 --> 00:01:30.026
Speak to us.

00:01:30.086 --> 00:01:32.946
It refuses to speak.

00:01:33.006 --> 00:01:35.427
I shall tell the prince.

00:01:35.487 --> 00:01:38.865
Perhaps the ghost will speak to him.

00:01:38.925 --> 00:01:41.513
This is a bad sign.

00:01:41.573 --> 00:01:46.225
Something sinister is happening in Denmark.

00:01:46.285 --> 00:01:50.157
Prince Hamlet is very sad.

00:01:50.216 --> 00:01:53.158
His father the king is dead.

00:01:53.218 --> 00:01:58.280
Gertrude his mother has married Claudius, his father's brother.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.802
Claudius has become the new king.

00:02:01.861 --> 00:02:05.794
Hamlet does not like his uncle.

00:02:05.854 --> 00:02:09.006
It is time to think about the future.

00:02:09.065 --> 00:02:14.500
I shall be a father to you, and you will be king after me, Hamlet.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.232
Stay here with us.

00:02:17.291 --> 00:02:20.594
Do not go back to university.

00:02:20.654 --> 00:02:23.035
We love you, Hamlet.

00:02:23.095 --> 00:02:26.037
I shall obey you, madam.

00:02:26.097 --> 00:02:30.600
My father was a better man than Claudius.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:35.773
My mother was weak and foolish to marry my uncle.

00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:40.004
Horatio comes to tell Hamlet about the ghost.

00:02:40.064 --> 00:02:44.936
Horatio has studied for many years with the prince at university.

00:02:44.996 --> 00:02:51.299
He is Hamlet's best friend, and the prince trusts him completely.

00:02:51.358 --> 00:02:55.170
I hate this place, Horatio.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.371
My uncle and my mother are so happy.

00:02:58.431 --> 00:03:02.492
How can they forget my father so soon?

00:03:02.552 --> 00:03:04.221
My lord.

00:03:04.281 --> 00:03:07.620
I saw your father last night.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.072
What do you mean?

00:03:10.132 --> 00:03:15.254
Come to the castle walls at midnight of the cliff.

00:03:15.314 --> 00:03:19.237
Then you'll understand.

00:03:19.297 --> 00:03:22.329
Hamlet sees the ghost of his father.

00:03:22.389 --> 00:03:25.080
It signals him to follow.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:28.592
I am your father's spirit.

00:03:28.652 --> 00:03:33.721
If you ever loved me, revenge my murder.

00:03:33.781 --> 00:03:36.049
Murder?

00:03:36.108 --> 00:03:41.042
My wife Gertrude was unfaithful to me.

00:03:41.102 --> 00:03:45.074
My brother Claudius murdered me.

00:03:45.134 --> 00:03:52.560
While I was sleeping in my garden, he poured poison in my ear.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.842
The sun is rising.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:04:00.530
I must go, Hamlet, remember me.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:04.466
Hamlet does not know what to do.

00:04:04.526 --> 00:04:07.917
Perhaps the ghost is telling lies.

00:04:07.977 --> 00:04:11.278
I shall pretend to be mad.

00:04:11.338 --> 00:04:16.790
Nobody will pay attention to a poor, crazy prince.

00:04:16.849 --> 00:04:20.630
I shall investigate my father's death.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:37.999
If the ghost's story is true, I shall kill my uncle.

00:04:38.058 --> 00:04:56.116
And so Hamlet, who was very intelligent, began to play the part of a madman.

00:04:56.176 --> 00:05:01.578
He did strange things, and he talked in a crazy way.

00:05:01.638 --> 00:05:07.579
He often said things with a hidden meaning which only he understood.

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:14.523
The people believed that Hamlet was mad, and they hoped that he would soon get better.

00:05:14.583 --> 00:05:20.370
The Queen was very worried because she loved her son.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:32.480
Only Horatio and the Gods knew the secret of Hamlet's meeting with the Ghost.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:38.576
Two.

00:05:38.636 --> 00:05:41.542
Hamlet and Ophelia.

00:05:41.602 --> 00:05:44.648
Ophelia lives at the castle.

00:05:44.708 --> 00:05:49.290
She has a brother, Laertes, who is studying in Paris.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:52.903
Ophelia is in love with Hamlet.

00:05:52.962 --> 00:05:58.846
One day, while she is sewing, Hamlet comes to her room.

00:05:58.906 --> 00:06:06.841
Later, she tells her father, Polonius, a foolish old lord about Hamlet's visit.

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:10.432
He looked so sad.

00:06:10.492 --> 00:06:14.282
He was only half-dressed.

00:06:14.342 --> 00:06:22.196
He stared at me, and then he left, without saying a word.

00:06:22.256 --> 00:06:26.179
Is he mad for your love?

00:06:26.238 --> 00:06:31.772
I don't know, but I think so.

00:06:31.832 --> 00:06:35.336
I must tell the king and queen.

00:06:35.396 --> 00:06:39.100
Polunius trusts Claudius in Gertrude.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:46.315
He has no idea that Claudius is a murderer or that Gertrude has been unfaithful to King Hamlet.

00:06:46.375 --> 00:06:51.608
Hamlet's love for my daughter has made him mad.

00:06:51.668 --> 00:06:53.600
That is possible.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:56.612
But how can we know for certain?

00:06:56.672 --> 00:07:01.324
We shall hide while Hamlet and Ophelia are talking.

00:07:01.384 --> 00:07:06.576
We shall listen to their conversation and discover the truth.

00:07:06.636 --> 00:07:10.499
You will see that I am right."

00:07:10.558 --> 00:07:14.480
Polonius gives instructions to Ophelia.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:21.010
He wants her to walk up and down the castle hall, reading her prayer book.

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:27.882
You must help us find out the truth about Prince Hamlet's madness.

00:07:27.942 --> 00:07:30.584
I shall obey you, Father.

00:07:30.644 --> 00:07:33.176
Quickly, here he comes.

00:07:33.236 --> 00:07:35.928
Pretend that you are reading.

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:39.930
Hamlet is thinking deeply.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:45.074
He wants to escape from his problems by committing suicide.

00:07:45.134 --> 00:07:48.857
His mind is full of questions.

00:07:48.916 --> 00:07:50.998
To be...

00:07:51.058 --> 00:07:53.560
Or not to be.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:57.223
That is the question.

00:07:57.283 --> 00:08:02.658
Is it better to live or die?

00:08:02.718 --> 00:08:07.501
But what happens after we die?

00:08:07.561 --> 00:08:10.743
Nobody knows.

00:08:10.803 --> 00:08:13.676
I am stupid.

00:08:13.736 --> 00:08:17.848
I must stop thinking and do something.

00:08:17.908 --> 00:08:22.063
I must discover the truth.

00:08:22.123 --> 00:08:27.297
But look, here comes Ophelia.

00:08:27.356 --> 00:08:30.228
Why is she standing there?

00:08:30.287 --> 00:08:33.388
Is it a trap?

00:08:33.448 --> 00:08:43.772
The prince is angry with Ophelia because he realizes that she is a spy for her father Polonius and King Claudius.

00:08:43.832 --> 00:08:46.842
I loved you once.

00:08:46.902 --> 00:08:50.104
I believed so.

00:08:50.164 --> 00:08:53.950
No, I never loved you.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.917
All women are stupid.

00:08:56.977 --> 00:09:01.908
They paint their faces and talk foolishly.

00:09:01.969 --> 00:09:05.460
Nobody should get married.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.952
Go away to a nunnery.

00:09:09.012 --> 00:09:14.704
The king does not believe that love is the reason for Hamlet's madness.

00:09:14.764 --> 00:09:17.926
He is very suspicious.

00:09:17.986 --> 00:09:22.543
Perhaps Hamlet knows my secret.

00:09:22.603 --> 00:09:24.669
We must watch him carefully.

00:09:24.689 --> 00:09:28.580
It is dangerous when a prince is mad.

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:31.692
Poor Hamlet.

00:09:31.752 --> 00:09:35.633
Everybody admired him before.

00:09:35.693 --> 00:09:39.474
He was the perfect prince.

00:09:39.534 --> 00:09:44.166
Now, his mind is ruined.

00:09:44.226 --> 00:09:53.302
Help him, sweet heavens.

00:09:53.362 --> 00:10:02.680
Hamlet enjoyed making fun of Polonius.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:11.198
One day, the prince was reading a book when he met the foolish old lord.

00:10:11.257 --> 00:10:14.028
What are you reading?

00:10:14.089 --> 00:10:18.113
Words, words, words.

00:10:18.172 --> 00:10:21.647
But what is the book about?

00:10:21.706 --> 00:10:23.469
It's full of lies.

00:10:23.528 --> 00:10:30.961
The writer says that old men are foolish, weak and have grey hair.

00:10:31.021 --> 00:10:34.308
Can you see that cloud, Polonius?

00:10:34.368 --> 00:10:35.698
Yes, my lord.

00:10:35.758 --> 00:10:38.350
It looks like a camel, doesn't it?

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:39.590
Yes, my lord.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.951
No.

00:10:41.011 --> 00:10:44.582
I think it looks like a weasel.

00:10:44.642 --> 00:10:46.953
Yes, my lord.

00:10:47.013 --> 00:10:50.765
Or perhaps it looks like a whale.

00:10:50.825 --> 00:10:53.346
Yes, my lord.

00:10:53.406 --> 00:11:00.986
Goodbye, you foolish old man.

00:11:01.046 --> 00:11:08.646
Three, the play.

00:11:08.706 --> 00:11:12.758
Two university friends come to visit Hamlet.

00:11:12.818 --> 00:11:17.280
Their names are Rose and Grant's and Guildenstern.

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:26.424
At first Hamlet is very pleased to see them, but they ask a lot of questions and he becomes suspicious.

00:11:26.483 --> 00:11:31.066
Why are you behaving so strangely?

00:11:31.126 --> 00:11:33.728
What's the matter with you?

00:11:33.788 --> 00:11:36.582
Tell us what you are thinking about.

00:11:36.642 --> 00:11:38.812
We are your friends.

00:11:38.872 --> 00:11:42.275
I think the king has sent them.

00:11:42.335 --> 00:11:45.426
They are spying on me.

00:11:45.486 --> 00:11:49.350
I shall not tell them anything.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:54.522
I cannot trust anyone except Horatio.

00:11:54.582 --> 00:11:58.485
Some travelling actors arrive at Elsinor.

00:11:58.545 --> 00:12:05.432
Hamlet loves the theatre, and he greets them like old friends.

00:12:05.492 --> 00:12:10.186
Welcome to Elsinor!

00:12:10.246 --> 00:12:14.578
We have come to perform a play for the king and queen.

00:12:14.638 --> 00:12:18.561
That gives me an idea, Horatio.

00:12:18.621 --> 00:12:23.384
I shall put some extra words in their play.

00:12:23.444 --> 00:12:29.808
I shall put the ghosts' story on the stage.

00:12:29.868 --> 00:12:35.017
That night, glorious and gertrude watch the play.

00:12:35.076 --> 00:12:37.104
There are three characters.

00:12:37.164 --> 00:12:43.800
The player king, the player queen, and Lucianos, the queen's lover.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.551
The murderer.

00:12:46.611 --> 00:12:50.674
I shall always love you.

00:12:50.734 --> 00:12:55.188
But if I die, you will marry again.

00:12:55.248 --> 00:12:58.240
No, never.

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:01.812
Do you like the play, Mother?

00:13:01.873 --> 00:13:05.189
The lady speaks too much about love.

00:13:05.249 --> 00:13:08.915
All the court of Denmark watch the play.

00:13:08.975 --> 00:13:15.700
Ophelia, Polodius, Horatio, Rosenkranzen, Guildenstern are all there.

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:24.696
But nobody knows the secret of King Hamlet's death, except Claudius and Hamlet.

00:13:24.756 --> 00:13:33.370
On the stage, while the player king is sleeping, the murderer pours poison in his ear.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:37.589
Hamlet, watch his Claudius' face carefully.

00:13:37.609 --> 00:13:42.762
This is the ghost's story.

00:13:42.822 --> 00:13:49.746
If Claudius is afraid, I shall know he is guilty.

00:13:49.806 --> 00:13:54.638
Suddenly, Claudius stands up and runs out of the court.

00:13:54.698 --> 00:13:57.138
Everybody follows him.

00:13:57.198 --> 00:14:01.259
The actors do not know what the problem is.

00:14:01.319 --> 00:14:04.889
Lights, lights, stop the play.

00:14:04.949 --> 00:14:07.540
Did you see that, Horatio?

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:09.771
The king is frightened.

00:14:09.831 --> 00:14:13.062
The ghost's story is true.

00:14:13.122 --> 00:14:19.585
After the play, Claudius feels very guilty, so he goes to pray in the chapel.

00:14:19.645 --> 00:14:23.017
Hamlet finds him there.

00:14:23.076 --> 00:14:27.828
I want God to forgive me for my brother's murder.

00:14:27.888 --> 00:14:31.900
Perhaps if I pray, he will help me.

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:36.153
It would be easy for me to kill him now.

00:14:36.213 --> 00:14:43.870
But if I kill him while he is praying, his soul will go to heaven.

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:47.374
I want him to go to hell.

00:14:47.434 --> 00:14:51.758
I shall wait for another opportunity.

00:14:51.818 --> 00:14:54.190
I cannot repent.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:15:02.079
God doesn't listen to my words.

00:15:02.139 --> 00:15:10.077
It's good to see you again, my friends.

00:15:10.137 --> 00:15:14.290
Let me give you some advice for the play tonight.

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:21.014
First of all, you shouldn't speak too loudly or too quietly.

00:15:21.074 --> 00:15:25.898
If the audience can't hear you, they won't be pleased.

00:15:25.958 --> 00:15:30.578
But if you shout, they won't like it.

00:15:30.638 --> 00:15:35.911
Secondly, you shouldn't move your hands too much.

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:42.575
But it's important to speak clearly so the audience will understand you.

00:15:42.635 --> 00:15:48.440
Next, remember to pay attention to the meaning of the words.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:58.558
Last of all, don't add any extra lines to the play and don't change the writer's words.

00:15:58.618 --> 00:16:03.492
I'll repeat all that because it's important.

00:16:03.552 --> 00:16:09.634
First of all, don't speak too loudly or too quietly.

00:16:09.694 --> 00:16:14.286
Secondly, don't move your hands too much.

00:16:14.346 --> 00:16:18.648
Thirdly, you should speak clearly.

00:16:18.709 --> 00:16:24.780
Next, you should pay attention to the meaning of the words.

00:16:24.839 --> 00:16:37.152
Finally, don't add any extra lines or change the words of the play.

00:16:37.212 --> 00:16:43.305
4.

00:16:43.365 --> 00:16:52.832
Murder and Exile It is the middle of the night, the time for witches and ghosts.

00:16:52.892 --> 00:16:56.737
Hamlet goes to see his mother in her bedroom.

00:16:56.797 --> 00:17:03.358
He does not know that someone is hiding behind the curtain and listening to everything.

00:17:03.418 --> 00:17:09.400
Hamlet, why did you offend the king?

00:17:09.461 --> 00:17:14.842
Mother, why did you betray my father?

00:17:14.902 --> 00:17:17.012
Don't move.

00:17:17.072 --> 00:17:19.689
I want to talk to you.

00:17:19.749 --> 00:17:25.298
I want to make you look into the mirror of your soul."

00:17:25.358 --> 00:17:30.570
The Queen is afraid of Hamlet and she begins to scream.

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:35.692
The spy behind the curtain shouts for help.

00:17:35.752 --> 00:17:42.656
Hamlet turns round quickly and without thinking kills the listener.

00:17:42.716 --> 00:17:45.150
Are you going to murder me?

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.330
Help!

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:47.912
Help!

00:17:47.972 --> 00:17:50.034
Help!

00:17:50.094 --> 00:17:51.144
What's that?

00:17:51.204 --> 00:17:52.416
Is it a rat?

00:17:52.476 --> 00:17:55.978
Is it the king?

00:17:56.038 --> 00:18:03.514
When Hamlet pulls back the curtain, he sees Polonius.

00:18:03.575 --> 00:18:05.636
Dead.

00:18:05.696 --> 00:18:08.638
What have you done?

00:18:08.698 --> 00:18:12.016
You have murdered Polonius!

00:18:12.077 --> 00:18:15.214
I thought it was the king.

00:18:15.274 --> 00:18:20.196
I'm sorry that I have killed this poor fool.

00:18:20.256 --> 00:18:24.658
But mother, I'm not as bad as you.

00:18:24.718 --> 00:18:29.602
You killed a king and married his brother.

00:18:29.662 --> 00:18:32.773
What do you mean?

00:18:32.833 --> 00:18:36.575
Suddenly the ghost appears in the room.

00:18:36.635 --> 00:18:42.515
He has come to remind Hamlet to take revenge before it is too late.

00:18:42.575 --> 00:18:49.784
Gertrude cannot see or hear him, so she thinks that Hamlet is crazy.

00:18:49.845 --> 00:18:55.136
Hamlet, don't hurt your mother.

00:18:55.196 --> 00:18:58.847
Remember that you must kill Claudius.

00:18:58.908 --> 00:19:02.398
Don't waste time.

00:19:02.458 --> 00:19:06.000
What is he looking at?

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:08.550
He's mad.

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:12.568
Oh, my poor son.

00:19:12.628 --> 00:19:15.626
Can't you see him, Mother?

00:19:15.686 --> 00:19:18.528
Don't you pity him?

00:19:18.588 --> 00:19:24.782
Hamlet, there is nothing there except the air.

00:19:24.842 --> 00:19:28.534
The ghost disappears.

00:19:28.594 --> 00:19:32.746
No, I'm not mad, Mother.

00:19:32.806 --> 00:19:36.455
Look at this portrait of my father.

00:19:36.515 --> 00:19:40.835
He was a good, brave, handsome man.

00:19:40.895 --> 00:19:46.549
Remember him and stay away from Claudius.

00:19:46.609 --> 00:19:50.392
I will, sweet Hamlet.

00:19:50.452 --> 00:19:57.818
But as soon as Claudius kisses you, you will forget everything and tell him my secrets.

00:19:57.878 --> 00:19:59.200
No.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:02.912
I promise not to betray you.

00:20:02.972 --> 00:20:05.996
I am glad, Mother.

00:20:06.056 --> 00:20:10.610
Now I must take away Polonius' body.

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:13.442
Good night.

00:20:13.502 --> 00:20:21.788
When Claudius hears that Hamlet has killed Polonius, he decides to send the prince away.

00:20:21.848 --> 00:20:24.159
Hamlet is dangerous.

00:20:24.219 --> 00:20:26.370
I shall send him to England.

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:31.219
Perhaps he will recover from his madness in a different country.

00:20:31.279 --> 00:20:39.281
Rosen, Cranston, Guildenstern, go with him and look after him.

00:20:39.341 --> 00:20:46.346
I shall send secret letters to the King of England.

00:20:46.406 --> 00:20:52.612
I shall tell the English to execute Hamlet as soon as he arrives.

00:20:52.672 --> 00:21:01.476
When he is dead, I shall be safe.

00:21:01.536 --> 00:21:09.759
It was a long journey by sea to England.

00:21:09.819 --> 00:21:17.084
One night, Hamlet could not sleep because he was thinking about all his problems.

00:21:17.144 --> 00:21:21.408
He got out of bed and walked around the ship.

00:21:21.468 --> 00:21:30.564
While Rosenkrantz and Guildenstern were sleeping, he stole Claudius' letter to the king of England.

00:21:30.625 --> 00:21:36.128
To his surprise, he read these orders.

00:21:36.188 --> 00:21:42.242
As soon as Hamlet arrives, cut off his head!

00:21:42.302 --> 00:21:46.686
Hamlet quickly prepared another letter.

00:21:46.746 --> 00:21:51.740
Execute the people who bring you this letter, he wrote.

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:53.930
He signed it.

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:56.603
Claudius.

00:21:56.663 --> 00:22:02.364
Then he went back to his cabin and hid the original letter.

00:22:02.424 --> 00:22:10.878
When Rosenkrantz and Gildenstern arrive in England, he thought, the English king will execute them.

00:22:10.938 --> 00:22:15.752
But how am I going to return to Denmark?

00:22:15.812 --> 00:22:29.768
The next morning, Rosenkrantz and Gildenstern woke up without realizing that the letter had been changed.

00:22:29.828 --> 00:22:36.128
Five.

00:22:36.188 --> 00:22:38.780
Suicide.

00:22:38.840 --> 00:22:44.802
Pollucius's son, Liatis, returns to Denmark from Paris.

00:22:44.863 --> 00:22:47.414
He is very angry.

00:22:47.474 --> 00:22:51.716
Claudius, you have killed my father.

00:22:51.776 --> 00:22:55.858
I shall persuade the people to rebel against you.

00:22:55.918 --> 00:22:58.590
There will be a revolution.

00:22:58.650 --> 00:23:00.731
No, Liatis.

00:23:00.791 --> 00:23:03.839
Hamlet is responsible for everything.

00:23:03.899 --> 00:23:06.877
But how did my father die?

00:23:06.938 --> 00:23:08.939
Why is it a secret?

00:23:08.999 --> 00:23:10.970
Be patient.

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:16.154
When I have explained everything, you will understand.

00:23:16.214 --> 00:23:18.656
I am your friend.

00:23:18.716 --> 00:23:21.878
Ophelia comes to see Liatis.

00:23:21.938 --> 00:23:26.010
She loved Hamlet, but he killed her father.

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:28.812
This has made her mad.

00:23:28.872 --> 00:23:34.978
She sings sad songs and gives flowers to everyone she meets.

00:23:35.038 --> 00:23:39.042
What is the matter with my sister?

00:23:39.102 --> 00:23:43.656
She has lost her mind, poor girl.

00:23:43.716 --> 00:23:49.210
He is dead, lady.

00:23:49.270 --> 00:23:52.463
He is dead.

00:23:52.483 --> 00:24:00.049
It will never come again.

00:24:00.109 --> 00:24:06.946
His bid was as white as snow.

00:24:07.006 --> 00:24:15.601
He is gone, he is gone.

00:24:15.661 --> 00:24:23.102
Love, remember me.

00:24:23.163 --> 00:24:27.033
Do you see this?

00:24:27.093 --> 00:24:29.963
Oh, God!

00:24:30.024 --> 00:24:33.834
A sailor brings a letter to Horatio.

00:24:33.894 --> 00:24:38.728
When he opens it, he discovers that it is from Hamlet.

00:24:38.788 --> 00:24:42.743
Horatio, I am in Denmark.

00:24:42.803 --> 00:24:45.574
Some pirates attacked our ship.

00:24:45.634 --> 00:24:50.018
While everybody was fighting, I jumped onto their ship.

00:24:50.078 --> 00:24:54.060
I paid them, and they brought me home to Denmark.

00:24:54.120 --> 00:24:58.592
Rosenkrantz and Guildenstern have continued to England.

00:24:58.653 --> 00:25:02.004
I shall tell you more about them when I see you.

00:25:02.064 --> 00:25:04.906
Meet me in the graveyard.

00:25:04.966 --> 00:25:07.056
Hamlet.

00:25:07.116 --> 00:25:10.297
I shall go to him immediately.

00:25:10.357 --> 00:25:13.470
I am glad he is safe."

00:25:13.530 --> 00:25:17.734
Claudius also receives a letter from Hamlet.

00:25:17.794 --> 00:25:21.457
He has a private conversation with Laertes.

00:25:21.517 --> 00:25:25.490
But why didn't you put Hamlet in prison?

00:25:25.550 --> 00:25:28.053
He is very popular with the people.

00:25:28.113 --> 00:25:30.516
It was impossible to punish him.

00:25:30.576 --> 00:25:33.757
The best thing was to send him to England.

00:25:33.817 --> 00:25:39.730
He has killed my father and driven my sister out of her mind.

00:25:39.790 --> 00:25:43.552
I would do anything to get my revenge.

00:25:43.612 --> 00:25:46.194
This letter is from Hamlet.

00:25:46.254 --> 00:25:48.476
He is back in Denmark.

00:25:48.536 --> 00:25:50.518
I'm glad.

00:25:50.578 --> 00:25:53.350
I will kill him.

00:25:53.410 --> 00:25:56.502
I have a better plan.

00:25:56.562 --> 00:25:59.524
The Queen comes in.

00:25:59.584 --> 00:26:03.820
I have bad news, Lettie's.

00:26:03.880 --> 00:26:07.154
Ophelia is dead.

00:26:07.214 --> 00:26:12.016
She wanted to put flowers on the willow tree.

00:26:12.076 --> 00:26:19.769
While she was climbing, she slipped and fell into the river.

00:26:19.828 --> 00:26:24.090
She floated there, singing.

00:26:24.150 --> 00:26:27.392
Then she drowned.

00:26:27.452 --> 00:26:31.294
Was it suicide?

00:26:31.354 --> 00:26:33.946
Nobody knows.

00:26:34.006 --> 00:26:37.862
Perhaps it was an accident.

00:26:37.922 --> 00:26:41.504
Oh, sweet Ophelia.

00:26:41.564 --> 00:26:45.138
I hoped she would marry Hamlet.

00:26:45.198 --> 00:26:50.582
Come, let us go and bury her.

00:26:50.642 --> 00:26:56.678
Now Hamlet has killed my father and my sister.

00:26:56.738 --> 00:27:00.751
Hamlet meets Horatio in the graveyard.

00:27:00.811 --> 00:27:03.576
They see a grave digger.

00:27:03.636 --> 00:27:09.722
He is preparing a new grave and he has uncovered some old bones.

00:27:09.782 --> 00:27:13.976
Hamlet begins to talk about death.

00:27:14.036 --> 00:27:17.108
Look at this skull, Horatio.

00:27:17.168 --> 00:27:19.440
It is Yorick's.

00:27:19.500 --> 00:27:22.702
He was the court jester.

00:27:22.762 --> 00:27:26.066
Alas, poor Yorick.

00:27:26.126 --> 00:27:28.668
I knew him, Horatio.

00:27:28.728 --> 00:27:33.756
When I was a child, he carried me on his back.

00:27:33.816 --> 00:27:36.950
His jokes were the best.

00:27:37.010 --> 00:27:41.791
He cannot make anybody laugh now.

00:27:41.852 --> 00:27:47.662
Perhaps this skull belonged to a beautiful lady.

00:27:47.722 --> 00:27:51.723
She cannot paint her face now.

00:27:51.784 --> 00:27:56.214
Perhaps this skull belonged to a lawyer.

00:27:56.274 --> 00:28:01.192
He cannot show how clever he is now.

00:28:01.252 --> 00:28:07.282
Perhaps this gulf belongs to a court gentleman.

00:28:07.342 --> 00:28:16.824
He cannot wear elegant clothes now.

00:28:16.884 --> 00:28:25.486
There is a willow by the river.

00:28:25.546 --> 00:28:31.151
Its silver leaves shine in the glassy water.

00:28:31.211 --> 00:28:40.258
Ophelia walked there, picking the flowers to hang on the graceful branches of the tree.

00:28:40.318 --> 00:28:54.391
But as she was climbing up to the sky, a thin branch broke under her small feet, and she fell down into the weeping brook.

00:28:54.451 --> 00:29:07.123
her dress spread wide, and, like a mermaid, she floated on the surface, singing old melodies.

00:29:07.183 --> 00:29:28.929
She was as happy as a creature of the water, but as her clothes grew heavy, they pulled her down to the dark bottom of the river, to muddy death.

00:29:28.989 --> 00:29:35.699
Six.

00:29:35.759 --> 00:29:39.592
The rest is silence.

00:29:39.652 --> 00:29:46.106
While he is standing in the graveyard, Hamlet sees a procession approaching.

00:29:46.166 --> 00:29:49.158
It is Ophelio's funeral.

00:29:49.218 --> 00:29:53.741
The queen throws flowers into the grave and says...

00:29:53.801 --> 00:29:56.082
Sweet to the sweet.

00:29:56.143 --> 00:29:59.795
Hamlet did not know that Ophelio was dead.

00:29:59.855 --> 00:30:01.746
He is shocked.

00:30:01.806 --> 00:30:06.718
He jumps into the grave and fights with Laertes.

00:30:06.778 --> 00:30:11.330
You killed my father and my sister.

00:30:11.390 --> 00:30:16.752
I loved Ophelia, more than 40,000 brothers.

00:30:16.812 --> 00:30:19.793
Laertes wants his revenge.

00:30:19.853 --> 00:30:24.384
He and Claudius decide how to kill Hamlet.

00:30:24.444 --> 00:30:28.356
You must challenge Hamlet to a fencing match.

00:30:28.416 --> 00:30:30.596
He loves this sport.

00:30:30.656 --> 00:30:32.796
He will certainly agree.

00:30:32.856 --> 00:30:34.147
Yes.

00:30:34.207 --> 00:30:38.129
And I shall put poison on the tip of my sword.

00:30:38.189 --> 00:30:42.351
If I cut him, he will die.

00:30:42.411 --> 00:30:49.934
And if this plan fails, I shall give Hamlet a poisoned drink.

00:30:49.994 --> 00:30:53.046
Hamlet accepts the challenge.

00:30:53.106 --> 00:30:56.376
He does not know about the poisoned sword.

00:30:56.436 --> 00:31:02.508
To him, the fight is just sport, something he enjoys.

00:31:02.568 --> 00:31:07.112
I am sorry for your father's death, Laertes.

00:31:07.172 --> 00:31:10.895
I accept your apology, Hamlet.

00:31:10.955 --> 00:31:15.118
Now, let's begin the fight.

00:31:15.178 --> 00:31:17.730
Here is a drink for you, Hamlet.

00:31:17.790 --> 00:31:21.524
If you're thirsty, good luck to you.

00:31:21.584 --> 00:31:25.940
I have bet six horses that you will win.

00:31:26.000 --> 00:31:30.996
Hamlet fights well and scores the first points.

00:31:31.057 --> 00:31:33.468
The Queen is very happy.

00:31:33.528 --> 00:31:36.519
She picks up the cup of poison.

00:31:36.579 --> 00:31:40.080
Claudius tries to stop her drinking.

00:31:40.140 --> 00:31:42.712
But it is too late.

00:31:42.772 --> 00:31:46.303
No, go through to do not drink.

00:31:46.363 --> 00:31:51.665
I drink to Hamlet.

00:31:51.726 --> 00:31:58.246
Lertie's wounds Hamlet with the poison sword.

00:31:58.306 --> 00:32:05.819
Later in the confusion, they exchange swords and hamlet wounds Laertes.

00:32:05.879 --> 00:32:10.272
The poison enters their blood.

00:32:10.332 --> 00:32:14.376
Suddenly, the queen screams in pain.

00:32:14.436 --> 00:32:19.670
Laertes falls to the ground and hamlet begins to feel weak.

00:32:19.730 --> 00:32:22.379
The poison is working.

00:32:22.439 --> 00:32:23.958
Help me!

00:32:24.018 --> 00:32:25.479
I am dying!

00:32:25.539 --> 00:32:27.581
We are all going to die.

00:32:27.641 --> 00:32:30.564
The sword and the drink were poisoned.

00:32:30.624 --> 00:32:33.496
The king is to blame.

00:32:33.557 --> 00:32:38.471
Then before I die, I shall have my revenge.

00:32:38.531 --> 00:32:42.324
This is for my father's murder!

00:32:42.384 --> 00:32:44.466
Treason!

00:32:44.507 --> 00:32:46.749
Treason!

00:32:46.809 --> 00:32:49.702
Hamlet is dying.

00:32:49.762 --> 00:32:55.456
Polunius, Sophia, latees, Gertrude and Claudius are all dead.

00:32:55.516 --> 00:32:59.558
It is time for a new beginning in Denmark.

00:32:59.618 --> 00:33:03.160
I shall kill myself too.

00:33:03.221 --> 00:33:05.392
No, Horatio.

00:33:05.452 --> 00:33:07.673
You must live.

00:33:07.734 --> 00:33:12.436
Tell the truth to the world after I am dead.

00:33:12.496 --> 00:33:15.544
Tell my story.

00:33:15.605 --> 00:33:19.728
Good night, sweet prince.

00:33:19.788 --> 00:33:42.724
And flights of angels sing thee to thy rest.

00:33:42.784 --> 00:34:04.290
Frailty thy name is woman.

00:34:04.350 --> 00:34:08.733
Something is rotten in the state of Denmark.

00:34:08.793 --> 00:34:10.925
Adieu.

00:34:10.985 --> 00:34:12.696
Adieu.

00:34:12.756 --> 00:34:14.858
Adieu.

00:34:14.918 --> 00:34:18.941
Remember me.

00:34:19.001 --> 00:34:27.215
One may smile and smile and be a villain.

00:34:27.275 --> 00:34:36.047
the plays the thing wherein I'll catch the conscience of the king.

00:34:36.108 --> 00:34:45.470
To be or not to be, that is the question.

00:34:45.531 --> 00:34:51.562
Madness in great ones must not unwatch to go.

00:34:51.622 --> 00:34:58.714
Suit the action to the word, the word to the action.

00:34:58.774 --> 00:35:01.744
My words fly up.

00:35:01.804 --> 00:35:04.446
My thoughts remain below.

00:35:04.506 --> 00:35:10.099
Words without thoughts never to heaven go.

00:35:10.159 --> 00:35:12.400
How now?

00:35:12.460 --> 00:35:13.771
A rat?

00:35:13.831 --> 00:35:15.652
Dead for a ducate?

00:35:15.712 --> 00:35:17.514
Dead?

00:35:17.574 --> 00:35:23.797
Thou turnst my eyes into my very soul.

00:35:23.857 --> 00:35:27.830
Sweet ladies, good night.

00:35:27.890 --> 00:35:30.017
Good night.

00:35:30.077 --> 00:35:36.972
Alas, poor Yorick, I knew him Horatio.

00:35:37.033 --> 00:35:43.142
There's a divinity that shapes our ends.

00:35:43.202 --> 00:35:47.508
The rest is silent.

